 contracts

Replay baseline: r6x author head 7316c7f9fae1bc4a0b7ab1848de0db4143eec5d2 and preceding
0500-series downstream patches. The original base and validation entries
below are historical provenance; r6x qualification is recorded separately.

Base: downstream steering stock-route and mHC-consumer optimization.
Rationale: execute the real ModelState and mHC host hooks on CPU with only
compiler/device imports substituted, then check the real consumer formula
against an FP64 oracle. Cover active residents outside the scheduled batch,
mixed rows, malformed controls, cancel/slot reuse, dummy capture identity,
FULL replay keys and per-route memory samples. Keep CUDA registration out
of the CPU fixture so GPU tests can import the actual operators afterwards.
Add SM12x tests of actual TileLang consume against the independent writer
projector across 101 dose updates in one graph, including zero-dose rows.
Quality: tests preserve strict stock bits and the existing numerical gate.
Validation: 104 CPU checks pass on macOS and local Linux CPU. The four
new SM12x cases and the existing GPU/serving checks are not executed in
this local-only work; CPU tests do not qualify CUDA kernels or throughput.
Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; not submitted upstream.

